*********************
* News in Version 2.3.1 (development)
*********************

* The package is renamed to localpsidR and the maintainer information is updated; the original credits and the license are kept.
* Fixed deprecated data.table syntax: with=FALSE combined with := raises an error since data.table 1.15.0 (a deprecated warning before), so build.panel() failed whenever a requested family variable was NA for a year.
* Added processPSID(), getFamilyPSID(), getIndPSID() and getPSID() for importing locally downloaded PSID files.
* Added support for the PSID 2023 wave: a new row in the wave tables, the crosswalk psid.xlsx updated, and famvars.txt/indvars.txt extended to 2019, 2021 and 2023.
* build.panel() no longer downloads data nor asks for PSID credentials; when files are missing it stops with a message that points to getPSID().
* build.panel() uses the newest IND<year>ER file when several are present, and gives a clear error when the individual file lacks the columns of the requested years or when a wave is not supported.
* getNamesPSID() now warns about years without a crosswalk column.
* Added exported extendVarsPSID() and the script data-raw/update-varlists.R to extend the variable lists to new waves.
* build.panel() has new arguments detect_waves (default FALSE) and head_code; getPSID() now writes psid_waves_detected.csv (metadata only) with the variable names it detects for waves that are not built in, and with detect_waves = TRUE build.panel() can build such a wave using those names, with a warning listing them. The built-in makeids() always wins.


*********************
* News in Version 2.1
*********************

* Updated to PSID to 2019 wave https://github.com/floswald/psidR/pull/45
* No longer support building with wealth variables. Those are included in the main family data file, and must be merged manually for early waves.


*********************
* News in Version 1.6
